---
// The privacy policy: what this site and the hosted version collect, who processes
// it, how long it's kept, and how to get it out or deleted. Self-hosted instances are their host's.
// Change UPDATED with the text, and keep the hosted section in step with fly/README.md.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Ink from '../components/Ink.astro';

const GITHUB = 'https://github.com/stevenmfarrell/concerninghabits';
const CONTACT = 'privacy@concerninghabits.com';
const UPDATED = 'October 18, 2026';

const providers = [
  { name: 'Cloudflare', what: 'Hosts this site, counts visits, and stores the hosted version’s backups', where: 'Worldwide; backups in the US' },
  { name: 'Fly.io', what: 'Runs the hosted version and keeps its database', where: 'US (Virginia)' },
  { name: 'Google', what: 'Sign-in for the hosted version, and its AI model (Gemini)', where: 'US' },
  { name: 'TypeSafe', what: 'Matches what you log to one of your habits', where: 'US' },
  { name: 'Sentry', what: 'Error reports, with personal data taken out', where: 'US' },
];
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy · Concerning Habits"
  description="What concerninghabits.com and the hosted version collect, who processes it, how long it’s kept, and how to get it out or deleted."
>
  <nav class="nav">
    <a href="/" class="home"><Ink art="plant-icon" class="home-plant" />Concerning Habits</a>
  </nav>

  <main>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated {UPDATED}</p>

    <section class="summary">
      <p>The short version:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Concerning Habits doesn’t sell your data, show ads or track you across other sites.</li>
        <li>A copy you host yourself sends us nothing. Its data stays on your server.</li>
        <li>On the hosted version, your habits are kept to run the app for you. You can download them or delete your account at any time.</li>
        <li>Questions or requests go to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <p>
      This policy covers what the Concerning Habits project (“we”) runs: this website at
      concerninghabits.com, and the hosted version at app.concerninghabits.com.
    </p>

    <h2>Self-hosted copies</h2>
    <p>
      Concerning Habits is <a href={GITHUB}>free software</a> you can run on your own server. A self-hosted copy
      doesn’t report anything to us. Its data is held and controlled by whoever runs it, and it goes only to the
      services they configure, such as the AI provider whose key they supply. If someone else hosts a copy for
      you, ask them about their own practices.
    </p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      The site has no accounts, no forms and no cookies. Cloudflare serves it,
      and like any web host it handles your IP address and browser details to deliver the pages and to block
      attacks. We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to count visits. It sets no cookies, doesn’t identify you, and
      only shows us totals such as page views, referring sites and countries.
    </p>

    <h2>The hosted version</h2>
    <p>The hosted version keeps what it needs to work:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Your account:</strong> your name, email address and Google account ID from Google sign-in, and
        your preferences, including your time zone so reminders arrive on time.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Early access:</strong> while the hosted version is open only to people we’ve invited, we keep
        a list of their email addresses to let them sign in. It’s deleted once sign-up opens to everyone.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>What you track:</strong> your habits, categories, entries, skips and vacations, and the people you
        share habits with.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Devices and connections:</strong> push-notification subscriptions for the devices you turn
        reminders on for, and any API keys and invites you create.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sign-in cookies:</strong> a cookie that keeps you signed in, and short-lived ones during Google
        sign-in. There are no advertising or analytics cookies.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>AI features</h3>
    <p>
      When you log something by typing, speaking or taking a photo, what you entered is sent to Google’s Gemini
      model, together with the names and details of your habits, so it can work out what you did. The text
      and your habit names also go to TypeSafe to pick the matching habit. Photos are sent for that one
      request and aren’t stored by us. Only the resulting entry is saved.
    </p>
    <p>
      Speech-to-text is done by your browser, not by us. Depending on your browser, your voice may go to its
      maker (Google for Chrome, Apple for Safari) to be transcribed.
    </p>

    <h3>Reminders</h3>
    <p>
      Reminders are sent through your browser’s push service (Google, Apple or Mozilla, depending on the
      browser), which receives the notification’s text to deliver it.
    </p>

    <h3>Error reports</h3>
    <p>
      When something breaks, a report goes to Sentry so we can fix it. Before it’s sent we remove request
      contents, cookies, headers, query strings and anything else that would show what you track. The report
      says where and how something failed, not who you are or what you logged.
    </p>

    <h3>Your data, and deleting it</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Download it</strong> at any time from Settings → Backup &amp; Restore, as JSON or CSV.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Delete your account</strong> from Settings → Delete Account. That removes your account and
        everything in it from the database straight away. Copies in our backups age out within about 30 days.
      </li>
      <li>
        Otherwise we keep your data for as long as you have an account. If you can’t sign in, email
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a> and we’ll handle the request for you.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who processes your data</h2>
    <p>We use these providers, each only for the purpose shown:</p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Provider</th><th>What for</th><th>Where</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {providers.map(p => (
            <tr><td>{p.name}</td><td>{p.what}</td><td>{p.where}</td></tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      Most of them are in the United States, so if you’re elsewhere your data is transferred there. Where
      the law requires it, these transfers rely on the providers’ standard contractual clauses or their
      certification under the EU–US Data Privacy Framework.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Wherever you live, you can ask us for a copy of your data, to correct it, to delete it, or to stop using it.
      We’ll answer within 30 days. If you’re in the EU, the UK or a similar jurisdiction, the legal bases we
      rely on are:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Contract:</strong> running the hosted version you signed up for.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Legitimate interests:</strong> keeping the site and app secure, fixing errors, and counting
        visits in aggregate.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You can also object to processing based on legitimate interests, and you have the right to complain to
      your local data protection authority.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      Concerning Habits isn’t meant for children under 13, and we don’t knowingly collect their data. If you
      think a child has signed up, email us and we’ll delete the account.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the date at the top changes too, and the history of every version is
      <a href={`${GITHUB}/commits/main/site/src/pages/privacy.astro`}>public on GitHub</a>. If a change
      significantly affects how we use data you’ve already given us, we’ll email you before it takes effect.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a> with any question or request about your data.
    </p>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <Ink art="plant-icon" class="footer-plant" />
    <a href="/">Home</a>
    <a href={GITHUB}>GitHub</a>
    <span>Free software under the AGPL-3.0 license</span>
  </footer>
</Base>

